From 89e80807695d3c340558ac24bc0993ead4372f64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toemmsen96 <147745097+Toemmsen96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:53:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] clk: qcom: gcc-msm8916: Add 26 MHz camera MCLK
 frequency

Camera sensors on MSM8916 phones are commonly clocked with a 26 MHz
MCLK, e.g. the Samsung S5K5E3 front camera of the Galaxy J5 whose PLL
settings assume a 26 MHz EXTCLK. The downstream Qualcomm/Samsung clock
driver provides this as F(26022000, gpll1_aux, 1, 1, 34), but the
mainline mclk0/mclk1 table (shared by both RCGs) only offers 9.6, 23.88
and 66.67 MHz.

GPLL1 runs at 884.736 MHz on MSM8916 (cf. the 294.912 MHz = GPLL1 / 3
gfx3d entry), so 26.022 MHz itself is not reachable exactly. The closest
rate the 5-bit half-integer pre-divider plus 8-bit M/N counter can make
is the plain integer division by 34 used downstream:

  884.736 MHz * 1 / 34 = 26.021647 MHz

which is 0.0014 % below the nominal 26.022 MHz and 0.083 % above 26 MHz.
Using M/N = 1/34 (an integer divider) also avoids the cycle-to-cycle
jitter of a fractional M/N setting such as GPLL0 / 2 * 13 / 200, which
would give exactly 26.000 MHz.

The table entry is labelled 26022000 like downstream, so that requests
for 26000000, 26021647 and 26022000 Hz all round up to it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8916.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8916.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8916.c
index 9c7c6b23c..24f032c8a 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8916.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8916.c
@@ -850,6 +850,8 @@ static struct clk_rcg2 jpeg0_clk_src = {
 static const struct freq_tbl ftbl_gcc_camss_mclk0_1_clk[] = {
 	F(9600000, P_XO, 2, 0, 0),
 	F(23880000, P_GPLL0, 1, 2, 67),
+	/* GPLL1 (884.736 MHz) / 34 = 26.0216 MHz */
+	F(26022000, P_GPLL1_AUX, 1, 1, 34),
 	F(66670000, P_GPLL0, 12, 0, 0),
 	{ }
 };
